## 2. Browser path — `transformers.js` + WebGPU

**`/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/web/src/stores/local-model.ts`** (550 lines) is the whole browser engine. It's a hand-rolled observable store class `LocalModelStore`, exported as a singleton `localModel` (line 550).

Loading (`performLoad`, ~line 268 onward) — **dynamic import** to keep the runtime out of the main bundle:

```ts
const { AutoProcessor, AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM, env } = await import(
    "@huggingface/transformers"
);

// Never attempt to resolve models from the app's own origin.
env.allowLocalModels = false;
env.useBrowserCache = true;
```

then:

```ts
const model = await AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(spec.id, {
    dtype: spec.dtype as any,
    device: "webgpu",
    progress_callback: (event: any) => { ... },
});
```

**Device is hardcoded `"webgpu"`** — there is no WASM fallback for the LLM path (unlike TTS). A `checkWebGpuAvailable()` preflight (line ~155) requests an adapter and additionally verifies the `shader-f16` feature before attempting the load, because every f16 export fails at session creation without it.

**Cancellation** is implemented by monkey-patching `env.fetch`, since `from_pretrained` takes no `AbortSignal`:

```ts
// `from_pretrained` takes no abort signal, but every request it makes
// goes through this hook, so cancelling really does stop the transfer.
const controller = new AbortController();
this.abortLoad = controller;
this.baseFetch ??= env.fetch;
const baseFetch = this.baseFetch;
env.fetch = (input: string | URL, init?: any) =>
    baseFetch(input, { ...init, signal: controller.signal });
```

There is an `epoch` counter (`loadEpoch`) so a superseded load's rejection is swallowed rather than surfacing as a failure banner.

**Inference** — `LocalModelStore.generate(prompt, options, onToken)` (line ~430):

```ts
const formattedPrompt = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(messages, {
    add_generation_prompt: true,
    enable_thinking: false,   // Gemma 4's thinking channel is noise here
    tokenize: false,
});
const { TextStreamer } = await import("@huggingface/transformers");
const streamer = new TextStreamer(tokenizer, {
    skip_prompt: true, skip_special_tokens: true,
    callback_function: onToken ? (text: string) => onToken(text) : undefined,
});
const outputs = await model.generate({ ...inputs, max_new_tokens: ..., do_sample, temperature, streamer });
```

So: **streaming yes**, via transformers.js `TextStreamer` token callback.

**No Web Worker.** I grepped — there is no worker anywhere in the local-model path. Generation runs on the main thread. (Keating *does* have a `SharedArrayBuffer` sandbox — `web/src/keating/nodepod-runtime.ts:233` — but that's "nodepod", an unrelated in-browser Node sandbox.)

